{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae5d-13b2-70c2-be9d-d3c6350c7765"},"sequence":66,"recorded_at":1780531400000127,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae5d-63d6-7d60-8ccc-db3bcf11553e"},"task_id":"01a0ae5d-63d6-7d60-8ccc-db3bcf11553e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae5d-63d6-7d60-8ccc-db3bcf11553e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-2-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls -la; echo \\\"===\\\"; cat AGENTS.md | head -50; echo \\\"===\\\"; ls internal/ 2>/dev/null; ls pkg/ 2>/dev/null; ls cmd/ 2>/dev/null\",\n  \"description\": \"List worktree root contents\",\n  \"exit_code\": 1,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"failed\",\n  \"terminal_reason\": \"process exited with status 1\",\n  \"output\": \"total 1432\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 20 iv  staff     640 Sep 17 07:43 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 iv  staff     128 Sep 10 07:42 ..\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff    6148 Sep 17 01:35 .DS_Store\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff      86 Sep  8 02:30 .git\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff     212 Sep  8 02:30 .gitattributes\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 iv  staff      96 Sep  8 02:30 .github\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff     191 Sep  8 02:30 .gitignore\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 11 iv  staff     352 Sep  8 02:30 .planning\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 iv  staff      96 Sep  8 02:30 .spec\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 13 iv  staff     416 Sep  8 02:31 .task-board\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 iv  staff     288 Sep 17 04:11 .temp\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff    6923 Sep  8 02:31 AGENTS.md\\nlrwxr-xr-x@  1 iv  staff       9 Sep  8 02:31 CLAUDE.md -> AGENTS.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff     712 Sep 17 01:20 go.mod\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff    5571 Sep 17 01:20 go.sum\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 31 iv  staff     992 Sep 17 09:46 internal\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff  466157 Sep 17 10:42 LOGBOOK.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff  205683 Sep 17 10:42 README.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff     276 Sep  8 02:31 Skillfile.json\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 iv  staff   11824 Sep 17 10:31 task-board.config.json\\n===\\n# Agent Session Manager Repository Instructions\\n\\n`AGENTS.md` is the canonical instruction file for this repository. `CLAUDE.md`\\nmust remain a relative symlink to this file so every supported agent reads the\\nsame rules.\\n\\n## Product and Specification\\n\\n- The product is Agent Session Manager, exposed as the `ax` command.\\n- Treat the [normative AX specification](https://github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec/blob/main/SPEC.md)\\n  as the authority for product behavior. Do not invent behavior that conflicts\\n  with it.\\n- This repository contains the implementation. Keep specifications and\\n  implementation changes traceable to their task-board work.\\n\\n## Change Workflow\\n\\n- Track every change in `task-board` before implementation begins. Keep the\\n  task status, checklist, notes, and task-scoped outcome evidence current.\\n- An authorized repository-changing task includes automatic delivery: stage\\n  only its reviewed scope, create author-signed commits, publish the feature\\n  branch, open or update the pull request, complete review and checks, and land\\n  the accepted exact head in `main`. Do not stop merely to ask whether the\\n  completed task should be committed, pushed, or landed.\\n- The repository bootstrap is the only direct-bootstrap exception. Every later\\n  change must be reviewed through a pull request. After approval and passing\\n  checks, land the exact signed feature head with a plain fast-forward push to\\n  `main`; never land through GitHub rebase, squash, or merge-commit actions.\\n- Never push unreviewed work, a different commit from the reviewed PR head, or\\n  a forced update to `main`. GitHub records the reviewed PR as indirectly\\n  merged when its exact head becomes reachable from `main`.\\n- Before creating a branch or worktree, fetch `origin`, switch to local `main`,\\n  and fast-forward it to `origin/main`. Never branch from stale `main`.\\n\\n  ```bash\\n  git fetch origin main\\n  git switch main\\n  git merge --ff-only origin/main\\n  test \\\"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" = \\\"$(git rev-parse origin/main)\\\"\\n  git switch -c <branch-name>\\n  ```\\n\\n- Use this signed linear landing flow after the PR is approved and its checks\\n  pass:\\n\\n  ```bash\\n  BRANCH=$(git branch --show-current)\\n  test \\\"$BRANCH\\\" != main\\n  git fetch origin\\n\\n===\\naxerror\\ncanonicaljson\\ncatalog\\ncataloggen\\ncigate\\ncliresult\\nconfig\\ndirnode\\nenviron\\nhostchannel\\nhosttrust\\ninvcore\\nlocalstore\\npeeridentity\\nprovhost\\nprovider\\nrpcwire\\nscalar\\nsecconftest\\nsecprim\\nsessadapter\\nsessquery\\nsessrepo\\nsessstate\\nspecdoc\\nspecpin\\nsshtransport\\nterminalbackend\\ntraceability\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3670,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 918,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
