ne. Two conforming readers of the same bytes\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-131-// disagreed, which is precisely the compatibility property this package exists\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-132-// to hold.\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-133-//\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-134-// The gate is the same one the CLI Result reader runs (cliresult.Decode), so\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-135-// both branches of a machine reading now enforce the same data model rather than\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-136-// one of them relying on the other to do it. It reaches every peer-supplied\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-137-// envelope through DecodeBound: provider, bridge, RPC, session-adapter and\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-138-// terminal-backend payloads are read here, so the duplicate-member shape is\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-139-// remotely reachable and is refused at the same place for all of them.\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-140-//\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-141-// Canonicalize's strict decoder settles more than duplicates - malformed UTF-8,\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-142-// lone or unpaired surrogate escapes, unescaped control characters in strings,\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-143-// trailing data after the top-level value, and more than 256 simultaneously open\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-144-// containers. Measured against the mutant that deletes this call, it is the only\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7564,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1891,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
