{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000db55","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae5d-13b2-70c2-be9d-d3c6350c7765"},"sequence":3077,"recorded_at":1780531400006149,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae94-609b-7860-9be8-3780fe81a165"},"task_id":"01a0ae94-609b-7860-9be8-3780fe81a165","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae94-609b-7860-9be8-3780fe81a165","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-72-1\",\n  \"command\": \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd = json.load(open('internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json'))\\nfor u in d['unowned_sections']:\\n    if u['key'] in ('section:11.10.1','section:11.10.2','section:11.10.3','section:11.10.4','section:11.10.5','section:6.6','section:16.1','section:11.10'):\\n        print('='*20); print(json.dumps(u, indent=1)[:2000])\\n\\\"; echo; grep -n \\\"reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256\\\\|ReviewedOwnership\\\\|func.*[Cc]anonical\\\" internal/traceability/traceability.go | head -20\",\n  \"description\": \"Show unowned host sections and pin mechanics\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"====================\\n{\\n \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.1\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.1 requires SSH host-channel launch with exclusive TLS 1.3, ALPN ax-host/1 and full mutual certificate authentication; no launcher, TLS endpoint or handshake exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-z1yxg9.\\\",\\n \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The repository carries no TLS, X.509 or SSH-launch code: provhost speaks the provider-plugin protocol over stdio, secprim checks argv, environment and paths, and the mesh RPC layer is catalog vocabulary without a transport.\\\"\\n}\\n====================\\n{\\n \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.2\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.2 requires certificate issuance into a machine-local trust store with enrolled roots and exact leaf checks; no issuance, store or enrollment implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\",\\n \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"No certificate, key custody or trust-store code exists: internal/config reads TOML only, internal/localstore keeps blobs and a SQLite projection, and the two new pin fixtures are byte identities without a Go consumer.\\\"\\n}\\n====================\\n{\\n \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.3\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.3 requires credential rotation, revocation and authorization generations that refuse stale trust; no rotation or revocation implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\",\\n \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Nothing in the tree rotates or revokes credentials: there is no credential store to rotate, no revocation list reader, and no authorization-generation check outside the specification text.\\\"\\n}\\n====================\\n{\\n \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.4\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.4 bounds host-channel assurance and executable fixture conformance; no assurance measurement or host-channel fixture runner exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\",\\n \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned host_channel_conformance fixture is a lock identity only: internal/secconftest runs crash, hostile and fuzz harnesses over local surfaces and reads no upstream conformance fixture.\\\"\\n}\\n====================\\n{\\n \\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.5\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.5 defines the upstream public synthetic admission validator, not a runtime requirement to parse SPEC.md during AX host admission. Its source vectors do not establish AX runtime conformance; production host-channel conformance remains pending. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\",\\n \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned section explicitly calls the predicates synthetic execution context and separates detailed DER, custody and runtime boundaries from policy witnesses. Upstream source publication ownership remains agent-session-manager-spec; TASK-260830-2x16gz owns consuming this evidence and proving real AX host admission.\\\"\\n}\\n\\n40:\\t// reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 pins the semantic JSON projection. JSON\\n43:\\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \\\"5102d3bce23e6f27264232332a300dbb89237dc7792673efe9ec039b1219ce08\\\"\\n437:\\tif gotDigest != reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 {\\n438:\\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"ownership registry projection digest %s differs from reviewed %s\\\", gotDigest, reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256)\\n778:func canonicalNumericSection(identifier string) string {\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3148,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 787,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
