{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dbb1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae5d-13b2-70c2-be9d-d3c6350c7765"},"sequence":3123,"recorded_at":1780531400006241,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae94-a31d-7fd1-bd79-9ba9f148d7e3"},"task_id":"01a0ae94-a31d-7fd1-bd79-9ba9f148d7e3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae94-a31d-7fd1-bd79-9ba9f148d7e3","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-74-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git show 244a7dc --stat | head -30; echo ===; git show 244a7dc -- internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json | head -120\",\n  \"description\": \"Show z1yxg9 traceability precedent diff\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"commit 244a7dce2f687c58238b1b11fbba67d618521632\\nAuthor: Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>\\nDate:   Thu Sep 17 11:53:25 2026 +0400\\n\\n    TASK-260830-z1yxg9: TASK-260830-z1yxg9: implement-rpc-envelope-and-hello\\n    \\n    Change-Request: CR-TASK-260830-z1yxg9-1 revision 1\\n\\n LOGBOOK.md                                       |   12 +\\n README.md                                        |   41 +-\\n internal/axerror/binding.go                      |    3 +\\n internal/axerror/binding_test.go                 |    3 +-\\n internal/hostchannel/README.md                   |  105 ++\\n internal/hostchannel/census_test.go              |  191 +++\\n internal/hostchannel/channel.go                  |  649 ++++++++++\\n internal/hostchannel/client.go                   |  282 ++++\\n internal/hostchannel/gates_test.go               |  112 ++\\n internal/hostchannel/hostchannel_test.go         |  516 ++++++++\\n internal/hostchannel/launch.go                   |   49 +\\n internal/hostchannel/launch_test.go              |  240 ++++\\n internal/hostchannel/mutations.py                |  130 ++\\n internal/hostchannel/refusal_test.go             | 1488 ++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/hostchannel/server.go                   |  394 ++++++\\n internal/hostchannel/verify_test.go              |  216 ++++\\n internal/rpcwire/README.md                       |   86 ++\\n internal/rpcwire/envelope.go                     |  259 ++++\\n internal/rpcwire/envelope_test.go                |  547 ++++++++\\n internal/rpcwire/hello.go                        |  147 +++\\n internal/rpcwire/inventory.go                    |   80 ++\\n internal/rpcwire/mutations.py                    |  121 ++\\n===\\ncommit 244a7dce2f687c58238b1b11fbba67d618521632\\nAuthor: Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>\\nDate:   Thu Sep 17 11:53:25 2026 +0400\\n\\n    TASK-260830-z1yxg9: TASK-260830-z1yxg9: implement-rpc-envelope-and-hello\\n    \\n    Change-Request: CR-TASK-260830-z1yxg9-1 revision 1\\n\\ndiff --git a/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json b/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json\\nindex 4d01fab..6ef3999 100644\\n--- a/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json\\n+++ b/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json\\n@@ -3670,7 +3670,7 @@\\n         \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.2; no clause of 11.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 5 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.2. TASK-260830-z1yxg9 adds rpcwire.DecodeRequest/DecodeResponse structural envelopes, request-ID/version correlation, 14-key hello maps, nonce echo and limit floors for RPC 2/3/4/5, and the hostchannel Serve/Dial authenticated hello consumer with its refusal table (internal/hostchannel, HC-HELLO/HC-DISPATCH families). No clause of 11.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 5 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n     },\\n     {\\n       \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n@@ -3685,7 +3685,7 @@\\n         \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3; no clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3. rpcwire now validates inventory.roots namespace/cardinality (6/7/8/8 across RPC 2/3/4/5) and matches roots to requested namespaces, and hostchannel dispatches authorized post-hello inventory.roots calls through the current-generation gate (TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel). No Merkle digest verification, schema membership or object exchange exists. No clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n     },\\n     {\\n       \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n@@ -3700,7 +3700,7 @@\\n         \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.8; no clause of 11.8 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 4 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.8. rpcwire pins the exact historical 24-key RPC-3 hello map and 7-namespace inventory syntax (contracts-v3 fixture); no negotiation, object exchange or clause of 11.8 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 4 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n     },\\n     {\\n       \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n@@ -3715,7 +3715,7 @@\\n         \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.9; no clause of 11.9 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 2 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.9. rpcwire pins the exact 25-key RPC-4 hello map and 8-namespace inventory syntax (contracts-v4 fixture) and reuses those shapes for RPC 5 with contracts.rpc [5.0.0]; no TerminalBackend evidence replication or clause of 11.9 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 2 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n     },\\n     {\\n       \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n@@ -3772,7 +3772,7 @@\\n         \\\"structured-error-common-data-model\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Two of the seven Section 15.1 clauses stay unimplemented here. Clause 15.1#5 is the RPC hello obligation - an error contract key must never be advertised or negotiated in a hello frame - and New builds a failure object rather than a hello frame; this repository contains no RPC hello builder at all, so BindingFor is a static table with no negotiation path rather than a refusal of one. Clause 15.1#6 is the Provider JSON-over-stdio bootstrap row, whose only RFC 2119 sentence is that the plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2; that obligation binds the provider plugin and this repository builds no provider plugin, only the cataloggen and tracecheck binaries. LocalFromUntrusted implements the host half of the same row, but that half states no RFC 2119 keyword, so it discharges nothing the clause scanner measures and is claimed for clause 15.1#7 instead.\\\",\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Two of the seven Section 15.1 clauses stay unimplemented here. Clause 15.1#5 is the RPC hello obligation - an error contract key must never be advertised or negotiated in a hello frame - and New builds a failure object rather than a hello frame; rpcwire now builds and rejects structural hello frames through its public codec and hostchannel consumes them in the authenticated handshake (Serve/Dial), while BindingFor stays a static table with no negotiation path; the clause itself is still not enumerated against an acceptance case. Clause 15.1#6 is the Provider JSON-over-stdio bootstrap row, whose only RFC 2119 sentence is that the plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2; that obligation binds the provider plugin and this repository builds no provider plugin, only the cataloggen and tracecheck binaries. LocalFromUntrusted implements the host half of the same row, but that half states no RFC 2119 keyword, so it discharges nothing the clause scanner measures and is claimed for clause 15.1#7 instead.\\\",\\n       \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n         {\\n           \\\"id\\\": \\\"15.1#1\\\",\\n@@ -3856,7 +3856,7 @@\\n         \\\"structured-error-exit-status-fan-in\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. No RPC hello frame is built anywhere in this repository, and the closed 16-capability admission registry in internal/terminalbackend is never advertised on an RPC hello path and carries no Structured Error code, so Section 15.3 keeps that clause unimplemented.\\\",\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit 