{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e33b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae5d-13b2-70c2-be9d-d3c6350c7765"},"sequence":4088,"recorded_at":1780531400008171,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae9b-74f1-71c1-8466-2f352c9a7d34"},"task_id":"01a0ae9b-74f1-71c1-8466-2f352c9a7d34","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae9b-74f1-71c1-8466-2f352c9a7d34","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-98-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -60 LOGBOOK.md; echo ...; grep -n \\\"^## \\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -8\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-z1yxg9 — RPC envelope/hello + Host Channel 1.0.0 implemented\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/rpcwire` completed for RPC 5.0.0 (exact RPC-4 shapes, contracts.rpc [5.0.0], Error statically 1.3.0 via a new axerror binding row) and `internal/hostchannel` built: mutual TLS 1.3 (exact ax-host/1, enrolled roots only, no tickets/cache/resumption), VerifyPeer supplement (ALPN presence, no-resume, verified chain, unique exact leaf/root/key match, profile, trust state), authorized hello both roles via hosttrust.AuthorizeDispatch, current-generation dispatch/mutation boundaries, one framed Error 1.3.0 refusal then close, silent close for unframeable input and foreign majors. Preserved pre-credentials packet restored verbatim (sha256-verified); UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS dropped as superseded by the v0.6.0 11.10 binding.\\n- F1: TLS 1.3 clients report handshake success before the server validates their flight, so rogue-cert refusal tests assert on the follow-up read, not the handshake call; the rogue must read (not write) first or the test deadlocks on the rendezvous pipe while the server blocks sending its alert. Production SSH pipes are OS-buffered and immune; the deadlock is a net.Pipe harness artifact.\\n- F2: Go wraps received TLS alerts as `*tls.permanentError` (unexported, implements net.Error with Timeout()=false) unwrapping to `*net.OpError{Op:\\\"remote error\\\"}`. The classifier maps Op==\\\"remote error\\\" to authentication_failed and every other OpError/timeout/EOF variant to transport_failure; matching on net.Error alone misclassifies alerts as transport.\\n- F3: `fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: %v\\\", sentinel, err)` formats the cause into the message WITHOUT chaining it; all 37 channel wraps now use `%w: %w` so errors.Is/As see both the refusal identity and the hosttrust cause. This one-character class of bug hid the identity-mismatch chain end to end.\\n- F4: Go caps handshake messages at 256 KiB, so the specified 1 MiB handshake byte cap cannot fire through a real TLS stack; it is unit-proven at the exact boundary (mutant-killed) and integration-proven as bounded intake (4 MB hostile preface reads < 64 KiB and fails fast). Unframeable reads now close the stream (found by the oversize-line test hanging on the half-open pipe).\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: hostchannel 1 neutral passed + 22 narrowing killed (incl. hello-ID substitution, stale-dispatch/mutation, cap+1, CA-bound+1, tickets, both TLS-min roles) + 1 documented harmless SURVIVED (client session cache without server tickets); token-preserving census-evasion mutant passes the static census and is killed by the runtime census with the full suite running. rpcwire 1 neutral passed + 34 narrowing killed (incl. new v5-exact). Per-probe overlays/logs/tables under /tmp/hcmut and /tmp/rwmut; packaged into the task outcome tar.\\n- VALIDATION: hostchannel + rpcwire green incl. -race; cover hostchannel 81.6/rpcwire 97.8; fuzz gate added to task-board.config.json and passing; axerror binding row + pinned tests updated; traceability gaps for 11.2/11.3/11.8/11.9/11.10/15.1/15.3 rewritten (coverage levels unchanged, no new clause discharge claimed) with reviewed digest 5102d3bce23e6f27264232332a300dbb89237dc7792673efe9ec039b1219ce08; README figures pin green.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 RPC rows driven through Serve/Dial/Call by named tests (see hostchannel README table). Stated bounds: no ax CLI/SSH launch/provider plugin (computed Config-4 argv only), SSH-carrier parity by construction (no SSH-impl branch), async one-second close via WatchGeneration polling, TLS alert text owned by crypto/tls. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev12 — exact interface call sites and side-effect-free binding refusal\\n- F1: the typed Config/Host Trust Store write-path census now allowlists interface edges by exact `*types.Func` identity plus source file/line/column, not by method spelling or enclosing-function membership. The inventory covers 119 production interface calls; the four pair-writer functions additionally require a top-level fail-fast hold guard before every admitted indirect write edge. Function-valued selectors and identifiers remain fail-closed except for named table entries; no non-callee interface method values were found in the production scan.\\n- F1 REGRESSION: `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` copies the module, plants real `filesystem.Rename` calls both before and after `requireHoldForConfig`, runs the real census, and proves the child rename witness executes before the census rejects both unlisted sites. The `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` mutant preserves the allowlisted method identity while dropping call-site/hold ordering, propagates its overlay into the child, and is killed by that production regression (child exit 0 under the mutant; outer test exit 1).\\n- F2: `ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates the store-side association and target-side association before publishing either side. A rejected second handle cannot leave a target claim behind; two handles opened before first binding publish exactly one winner; an interrupted first binding repairs the missing store index on reopen. RED evidence is `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/rebind-red-rev12.log`; the fixed production tests are `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: batteries rerun in full on the post-refresh final tree: Config4 1 neutral + 13 killed, Host Trust Store 1 neutral + 34 killed, 0 survivors (47 killed total, every kill exit 1 with the expected named test failing). Runs split into 9 bounded groups with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; per-mutant overlays/results/tables are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-*-rev12post-group*` (pre-refresh partial runs under `mutations-*-rev12-*` agree). Generated `__pycache__` bytecode was removed.\\n- VALIDATION (final tree, head `5e54874`): `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 all packages ok (4m40s); cover config 92.9/hosttrust 76.3/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4/localstore 83.8; `-race` on hosttrust+config exit 0; `go vet`, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, `git diff --check` clean; native + darwin/linux/windows builds exit 0; Windows test-compile + vet exit 0 (no runtime claim). F1 gate + call-site regression pass; F2 trio passes post-fix and the rebind test fails RED (exit 1) on unfixed CR11 code. Full logs and board evidence are in the rev12 outcome package.\\n- PRESERVATION/SCOPE: base moved by managed refresh-candidate to trunk `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e` (replayed checkpoints `efe119a`/`5e54874`); candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree. RPC backup/parked delta and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain outside this leaf. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; native Windows runtime ACL and downstream export/diagnostic consumers are explicit bounds. No RPC behavior, main integration, or review acceptance is claimed.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev11 — opaque resolved pair and current negative evidence\\n- F2: all pair-bearing production boundaries now consume the opaque `localstore.ResolvedPaths` minted by the single `localstore.ResolvePaths` resolver. `hosttrust.Open`, binding/hold validation, `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, Config4 preview/apply/rollback, legacy migration, and pair writers no longer accept caller-supplied config/state tuples. The target-side binding record is authoritative; reopening a store with a derived binding but a missing target record refuses closed. The foreign-store target-binding probe is narrowing and killed by `TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreWithTargetBinding`.\\n- F1: the write-path census now compares exact `*types.Func` interface-method objects and rejects unlisted interface/type-parameter calls, parenthesized callees, and method values; executable real-file witnesses cover the new shapes. The preserved-token `writepath-interface-name-heuristic` mutant runs the behavioral suite and is killed.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: current Config4 battery has 1 neutral control plus 13 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed (exit 1 with named production failures; `config-association-root-skip` was rerun in `part4b` and counted once). Current Host Trust Store battery has 1 neutral control plus 34 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed. One first-pass `hold-state-root-skip` compile failure was a harness defect; the corrected mutant rerun killed `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsForeignConfigStateRoot`, and the failed instrument run is not counted.\\n- VALIDATION: fresh `internal/config`, `internal/localstore`, `internal/hosttrust` tests, `go test ./... -v`, `go test ./... -cover`, `go vet ./...`, native/cross `go build`, cross test compilation with `go test -exec /usr/bin/true ./... -run '^$'` for darwin/linux/windows, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, and `git diff --check` pass. The ordinary cross `go test -run '^$'` execution lane is retained as an expected host-format limitation (bad CPU/exec format), not a code pass.\\n- PRESERVATION/HANDOFF: RPC backup 15/15 and parked delta 11/11 remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work is untouched; no RPC path was absorbed. Candidate remains UNCOMMITTED at `HEAD=305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` on protected `origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; Windows runtime ACL (row 15) and downstream export/diagnostic consumers (row 21) are explicit bounds. Ready for developer-to-reviewer handoff; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev10 — Config4 binding and typed write-path census closed\\n- BASE/PRESERVATION: candidate was verified on current protected AX trunk (`origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`, worktree HEAD `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`). The 15-file RPC backup and 11-file parked RPC delta remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work remains present and no RPC implementation path was absorbed. Candidate changes remain UNCOMMITTED for the managed Story handoff.\\n- F1: Config4 now has an immutable, owner-only `config-binding.json` sidecar. Binding is explicit through `EnsureConfigBinding`; `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, and pair writers require the existing binding and reject a missing, malformed, unreadable, rebound, or foreign state-root binding. The config-side selected `StateRoot` is compared to the canonical Host Trust Store root; no non-normative Config4 field was added to the closed `mesh.host_channel` table. `OpenForConfig` and the implicit legacy fallback were removed.\\n- F2: the write-path census is typed and fail-closed: unresolved calls, non-`*types.Func` call targets, and unlist