ation transaction (`openLegacyStore` + `WithExclusiveHold` + `revalidateLegacySource` + token-gated `replaceDurably`): legacy writers serialize with joint commits and refuse `ErrMigrationStaleSource` when the source moved. Rev6 unlocked exemption deleted; pre-hold refusals write nothing; opening creates the owner-only skeleton when absent (documented) and fails closed when unopenable. Sync CR6 probe RED pre-fix; post-fix it blocks on the held lock (timeout dump proves the hold, CR5-restore precedent) and the committed async port `TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4` pins serialize-then-refuse-stale + fresh Config4 commit.\\n- F2: `JointCommit` routes replace errors through `resolveFailedReplace` (pin-verified: source-intact aborts with the original error, durable/diverged/unreadable runs compensation restore-or-keep-marker). Both CR6 probes RED pre-fix, green post-fix; marker-kept reopen/forward tests added for apply + rollback (`TestApplyV4FailedReplaceKeepsMarkerWhenRestoreFails` + rollback twin, `TestResolveFailedReplaceKeepsMarker`).\\n- F3/INSTRUMENT: `hosttrust.HeldExclusive` capability (only `exclusiveHold` forges; verified live pre-write; expired on unlock) threaded through all pair writers; `store.lock.exclusive()` signature kept for read paths and probe compat. Static gate rewritten fail-closed (all decls incl. package-var initializers, transitive alias resolution, helper-escape detection, exact (receiver,method) backend pairs, direct-os-mutation rule, hold-entry closures for JointCommit+WithExclusiveHold) with 6 executable rogue controls (4 reviewer verbatim + direct-os.WriteFile + backend-receiver rogue); rev6 token-less plants no longer compile (vet error captured as evidence).\\n- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 33 killed (32 narrowing + 1 call-site) + neutral passed; config 10 killed (9 semantic + 1 label-precision) + neutral passed; new plants hold-require-skip, hold-no-lock, resolve-source-skip, replace-require-skip, legacy-revalidate-skip, replace-restore-skip (each admits exactly one member; kept halves verified in plant logs). Full local validation green: 26/26 packages ok, race ok, cover hosttrust 78.0/config 93.5/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4, 343 top-level PASS 0 FAIL across touched packages, fuzz 13/13, tracecheck/catalog/cigate/JSON/diff-check clean, task-board validate exit 0 with 0 issues for this task. 7 original + 2 F2 exact probes pass on final source. 19/21 AC rows driven, all passing; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5/CR6.\\n- LESSON: intermittent \\\"package X is not in std\\\"/\\\"could not import\\\" battery failures were external go-build-cache interference (different plants each run; serial re-runs kill); batteries re-run with a private GOCACHE. Never run concurrent `go` commands during overlay batteries on this machine.\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\\n- F1: `JointCommit` takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked`): marker re-read pin-for-pin, config hash must equal the replacement pin, restore result verified against the source pin before the abort. No reader/writer/boundary can converge between failure and restore. The unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted. Original CR5 probe RED (exit 1, quoted failure) pre-fix; post-fix its in-seam convergence blocks in `flock` (timeout dump proves the hold) and the ported `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\\n- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`