A rejected second handle cannot leave a target claim behind; two handles opened before first binding publish exactly one winner; an interrupted first binding repairs the missing store index on reopen. RED evidence is `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/rebind-red-rev12.log`; the fixed production tests are `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: batteries rerun in full on the post-refresh final tree: Config4 1 neutral + 13 killed, Host Trust Store 1 neutral + 34 killed, 0 survivors (47 killed total, every kill exit 1 with the expected named test failing). Runs split into 9 bounded groups with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; per-mutant overlays/results/tables are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-*-rev12post-group*` (pre-refresh partial runs under `mutations-*-rev12-*` agree). Generated `__pycache__` bytecode was removed.\\n- VALIDATION (final tree, head `5e54874`): `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 all packages ok (4m40s); cover config 92.9/hosttrust 76.3/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4/localstore 83.8; `-race` on hosttrust+config exit 0; `go vet`, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, `git diff --check` clean; native + darwin/linux/windows builds exit 0; Windows test-compile + vet exit 0 (no runtime claim). F1 gate + call-site regression pass; F2 trio passes post-fix and the rebind test fails RED (exit 1) on unfixed CR11 code. Full logs and board evidence are in the rev12 outcome package.\\n- PRESERVATION/SCOPE: base moved by managed refresh-candidate to trunk `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e` (replayed checkpoints `efe119a`/`5e54874`); candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree. RPC backup/parked delta and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain outside this leaf. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; native Windows runtime ACL and downstream export/diagnostic consumers are explicit bounds. No RPC behavior, main integr