8.0/config 93.5/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4, 343 top-level PASS 0 FAIL across touched packages, fuzz 13/13, tracecheck/catalog/cigate/JSON/diff-check clean, task-board validate exit 0 with 0 issues for this task. 7 original + 2 F2 exact probes pass on final source. 19/21 AC rows driven, all passing; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5/CR6.\\n- LESSON: intermittent \\\"package X is not in std\\\"/\\\"could not import\\\" battery failures were external go-build-cache interference (different plants each run; serial re-runs kill); batteries re-run with a private GOCACHE. Never run concurrent `go` commands during overlay batteries on this machine.\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\\n- F1: `JointCommit` takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked`): marker re-read pin-for-pin, config hash must equal the replacement pin, restore result verified against the source pin before the abort. No reader/writer/boundary can converge between failure and restore. The unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted. Original CR5 probe RED (exit 1, quoted failure) pre-fix; post-fix its in-seam convergence blocks in `flock` (timeout dump proves the hold) and the ported `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\\n- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`; preserve-token order-swap plant `compensate-verify-before-restore` passes the gate and fails only behaviorally.\\n- INTERLEAVINGS: 6 deterministic gated-restore race tests (apply/rollback × reader/writer/held-boundary) + 2 production-entry clean-abort tests + 8 hosttrust compensation tests (tamper/corrupt/unreadable marker, noop+wrong-bytes restore verification, fail-after-write, source-present skip). TEST BUG FOUND BY RACE SUITE ITSELF: boundary tests deadlocked reading trust post-seam on the main goroutine — request now binds pre-seam with a comment.\\n- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 29 narrowing (incl. 4 compensate-*) + 1 call-site + neutral passed; config 6 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; all plants pre-verified count==1 with exits from subprocess return codes. Full local CI replicated green (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 pre-existing SKIP; race 26 ok; cover hosttrust 77.9/config 93.3; tracecheck/catalog-6/cigate-contracts-6/claims-6/targets-2/fuzz-13/fixtures 51+59 zero-skip/windows-compile). 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5.\\n- BOUNDS RESTATED: verifyLockFile 500ms retry rechecks custody without pinning an inode (no external-replacement claim); power-loss beyond fsync unproven; Windows runtime unverified; diagnostics export unowned; spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\\n...\\n6:## 2026-09-17\\n18:## 2026-09-17\\n28:## 2026-09-17\\n46:## 2026-09-16\\n69:## 2026-09-10 (refresh)\\n78:## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n90:## 2026-09-10\\n101:## 2026-09-17\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 18391,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4598,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
