{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000eb07","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae5d-13b2-70c2-be9d-d3c6350c7765"},"sequence":5086,"recorded_at":1780531400010167,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d399377e-e1e6-462b-bf26-c7cdc6c1ce28"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to `to-review` (checklist 14/14, three outcome resources attached).\n\n## What was delivered\n\nTest-only final leaf, no production file changed. Worktree left uncommitted at `244a7dc` on the Story branch.\n\n- **Conformance suite** ([hostile_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree/internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go), [hostile_carrier_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree/internal/hostchannel/hostile_carrier_test.go)): all seven hostile cases re-derived through real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, plus AC-HOST-001 rows — real OpenSSH loopback lane (exact `ServeArgv` observed server-side, TLS-first, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, v4 loader gate. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\n- **Coverage**: 7 of 7 hostile rows, 14 of 15 AC-HOST-001 rows fully driven (B8 partial — see bound), 10 of 10 HC-* families, production call site named per row in the matrix.\n- **Mutants**: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named tests (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); 26 prior probes re-run green.\n- **Story-close**: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 tests; bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1; 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 unowned by design; digest re-pinned; README/package docs + LOGBOOK updated with no capability claims.\n\n## Key findings\n\n- When the *server* refuses mid-handshake, `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` while `Serve` reports `authentication_failed` (TLS 1.3 early completion + rendezvous) — both sides pinned.\n- Measured bound: an idle stream with zero traffic does **not** self-close within 1s of revocation (no watchdog in `serveLoop`); next-dispatch fence + `WatchGeneration` measured < 1s. Recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\n- Validation all green: full suite + race + cover (31 pkgs), 14 fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, cross-builds, vet/gofmt/diff-check.\n\n## Note for the orchestrator\n\n`task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution); the worktree was left untouched. `task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to the checkpoint (untouched); vs trunk it differs only by the expected z1yxg9 fuzz gate plus trunk drift from `c5582bc`.","reason":null}}
